error[E0409]: `g` captured `term`, an authority, so it may be called only once, but `twice` may call it more than once
  --> single_use.ck:20:9
   |
20 |     let g = \_ -> say "hello" term
   |         ^
   = help: pass `term` to the closure as a parameter, so that each call is given it

error[E0409]: a closure that captured `term`, an authority, may be called only once, but here it may be called more than once
  --> single_use.ck:53:12
   |
53 | fn to_many term -> r : term~Term, r~Unit
   |            ^^^^
   = note: a closure that captured `term` is passed to `many`, whose parameter is not `own`, so `many` may call it any number of times
   = help: pass `term` to the closure as a parameter, or mark that parameter of `many` with `own` (as in `f~own (Unit -> a)`)

